claim.claim-text:
- transportation means (17) for removing in an ordered manner the capsules filled with product from the handling carousel (14) and means (40) for cyclically deviating the said capsules towards statistical weight checking means (41 ) which emit an electrical signal proportional to the weight detected; 

- a processor (39) with associated programming, interrogation and recording unit (139), which governs automatic operation of the metering machine which among other things receives the electrical signals supplied by the said statistical weight checking means and compares them with predetermined reference values, within which the capsules are considered suitable for use and then conveyed away towards the usable product line (42), and outside of which the said capsules are deviated towards a reject line (43), while the processor performs any correction in the volume of the metering seats and any correction in the heightwise position of the pressing thrusters or rams, characterized by the fact that at least the thrusters (6) for pressing the metered amounts of product inside the hollow-punch metering devices or at least the rams for final pressing of the product inside the holes of the metering disc have, associated with them, force transducers (T) which emit an electrical signal proportional to the thrust which the said thrusters or rams exert on the metered amount of product being pressed and means (44, 45) are provided for amplifying, for processing and for transferring this signal to the processor (39) which compares it with predetermined parameters relating to an acceptable weight condition for the metered amounts of product, outside of which parameters the processor causes emission of an alarm signal, performs any adjustment or automatic adjustment of the packaging machine and causes in synchronism the deviation, towards a reject flow (43), of the capsules containing the metered amounts of product which are not acceptable by means of switching means (46) operating downstream of the unloading station of the carousel (14) handling the capsules. 2. Apparatus according to Claim 1 , characterized in that it comprises precision means (49) for checking, also by means of sampling, the mass or weight of the capsules rejected by the switching means (46) operating downstream of the unloading station of the capsule handling carousel, and for transmitting to the processor (39) an electrical signal proportional to the weight detected, so that this control unit is able to check the operation of the force transducers associated with 

the pressing thrusters or the final pressing rams and, where necessary, must modify the processing parameters of the signal emitted by these components in the event of* the precision check revealing that the capsules do have an acceptable weight.
